# The maintainers' deployment values that redaction.py looks for in every clone and in CI (#248),
# as the first hex digits of SHA-256("colvenna-lake-redaction:" + the value in lowercase). The values are
# never written here. A line is <account|text> <hex digits> <what the value is>; make one with
#   redaction.py --hash < a file with the value
# An account keeps 6 digits, so that the line does not give it away; any other value keeps 16.
# Not here: values one can guess and then check against a hash (the hosted zone's domain, built on
# the repository owner's public name; the executor's role name). The settings in deploy/.state
# hold them on the maintainers' machines, where the check reads them.
account 559928 the maintainers' work account
text a171d7feb63458b2 the ID of the maintainers' hosted zone
text 993aaa5192dfe6a6 the EC2 instance of the maintainers' executor
